    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d948">

                <pb facs="0806" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Stuart, J. Leighton: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-22T21:00:00+08:00">July 22, 1949—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:30 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 801. Urge desirability advance information Canton for release here at
                    proper time by Connors<anchor n="27" xml:id="d948-f1"/> of publicity
                    contemplated Deptel 825, July 20 to Nanking, repeated Canton telCan 470. Advance
                    knowledge details Department’s plans and <hi rendition="#italic">en clair</hi>
                    message re release would be most valuable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d948-f1" n="27" xml:id="d948-f1-content">
                <p>W. Bradley Connors, Attaché in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
